title: 'k8s_apply cannot update an existing custom resource: fallback is hard-wired
  to strategic merge patch (415)'
updated: 2026-10-19T20:31:38Z
---

After a 409 on create, `k8s_apply` patches with `type => 'strategic'` unconditionally (lib/MCP/K8s.pm:1546-1552) and offers no `patch_type` parameter. The same file documents that custom resources answer a strategic merge patch with 415 (lib/MCP/K8s.pm:1201-1202, POD 825-832; Kubernetes::REST patch_status POD says the same), and `k8s_patch subresource=status` defaults to merge for exactly that reason. So 'create or update' works for built-ins only: for any CRD kind the second apply ends in 'Failed to update Kind/name: 415 ...'. The module advertises CRD support through the generic tools.

Not run against a cluster (no network in this review); follows from the code plus the API server behaviour the dist itself documents.

Done when: the fallback picks merge patch for kinds that are not built-in (e.g. class is IO::K8s::Unstructured / not under IO::K8s::Api::, or retry with merge on 415), with a mock test; alternatively expose `patch_type` on `k8s_apply`.

